    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0665" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg571"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to the
                            Acting Secretary of State of the South African
                            Republic.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Highly appreciate your courteous cablegram of to-day. Contents are noted. Take
                    this opportunity to commend to your gracious consideration arrested Americans,
                    who, if they have inadvertently given your Government any cause for complaint,
                    must certainly be acquitted of all complicity in any political designs against a
                    Republic for which the United States can bear only the friendliest feelings.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
